    "result": "Perfect! The feature is complete and fully tested. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n### 1. **Added `renderSummary(result: GateResult): string` function**\n   - Location: `packages/frai-gate/src/gate/report.ts`\n   - Returns format: `<VERDICT> <answered>/<total>` where total = 7\n   - Answered = number of checks with no block findings (warnings don't reduce this count)\n   - Special case: Returns `BLOCK 0/7: structure` when gate section is missing\n   - Appends `: check-id-1, check-id-2` for any block findings, in GATE_CHECKS order\n   - Exported from public API via `src/index.ts`\n\n### 2. **Added `--summary` flag to `frai-gate check`**\n   - Prints only the one-line summary instead of full report\n   - Exit codes remain unchanged (1 for BLOCK, 0 for PASS/WARN)\n   - `--json` takes priority if both flags provided\n   - Documented in HELP text\n\n### 3. **Added comprehensive tests** (`src/gate/report.test.ts`)\n   - 8 tests covering all verdicts, edge cases, and ordering\n   - All 19 tests passing (11 existing + 8 new)\n\n### 4. **Build & Test Results**\n   - \u2705 Build successful: `pnpm --filter frai-gate build`\n   - \u2705 All tests pass: `pnpm --filter frai-gate test`\n\nThe feature is production-ready and works as demonstrated:\n- `PASS 7/7` for fully answered specs\n- `BLOCK 5/7: risk-tier, data-privacy` for specs with block findings\n- `BLOCK 0/7: structure` when gate section is missing\n- `WARN 7/7` for specs with only warnings",
